<title>UK: UBS leads $50 mln emerging market-linked bond.</title>
<headline>UBS leads $50 mln emerging market-linked bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>UBS said on Friday it had lead managed a $50 million bond for special purpose vehicle SPARC EM Ltd linked to emerging market bonds.</p>
<p>The bonds, which mature on June 20, 2002, pay a 14.75 percent semi-annual coupon and are priced at par.</p>
<p>They are secured by an interest rate swap with UBS London Branch and an equal dollar weighted portfolio the following emerging market bonds:</p>
<p>- Argentina 8.75 percent BONTES due 2002,</p>
<p>- Banco do Brasil 8.375 percent due 2002,</p>
<p>- Pemex 8.5 percent due 2002,</p>
<p>- Ecuador 11.25 percent due 2002,</p>
<p>- Russia 9.25 percent due 2001,</p>
<p>- Turkey 10.0 percent due 2002.</p>
<p>Payment date is July 16. The notes are sold in denominations of 100,000 and selling restrictions apply in Britain, the U.S. and the Cayman Islands.</p>
<p>The notes are callable subject to the occurrence of a threshold test failure, UBS said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
